course: dictionary
lesson: 5872
title: The mandrill: a monkey with a painted face
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mandrill is a large monkey from the rainforests of central Africa. You may not know that word yet, but the sentences around it can help. «Male mandrills have the brightest faces of any monkey, bright blue and red» tells you that the mandrill's face is coloured, and that bright colours belong to the males.
explain: «There are hundreds of kinds of monkeys, from a pygmy marmoset that could sit on your finger to a mandrill heavier than a big dog.» The words "from... to..." show you a range, from the tiniest to the biggest. Since the mandrill is the heavy one, you can work out that it is a big monkey.
explain: Clues can also show why an animal does something. «Mandrills have very long canine teeth, and a wide yawn shows them off as a warning to rivals.» Here the yawn is not a sign of being tired. It is a way of saying, "Keep away," so a yawn can be a warning.
fact: A mandrill is a large monkey from the rainforests of central Africa.
fact: Male mandrills have bright red and blue faces, and the most colourful males are often the strongest.
fact: Mandrills are the largest monkeys in the world, and they live in big groups called hordes.
fact: Mandrills eat fruit, seeds and insects, and they have very big teeth.
fact: In «The Lion King», Rafiki is partly based on a mandrill, which is why he looks wise and a little funny.
exercise: «Mandrills, the monkeys with red and blue faces, live in the rainforests of central Africa, not on the open savanna.» Where do mandrills live? | On the open savanna | *In the rainforests of central Africa | On farms in the desert | In the mountains of Europe
exercise: «Mandrills have very long canine teeth, and a wide yawn shows them off as a warning to rivals.» Find and copy the word that means competitors. | teeth | warning | *rivals | yawn
exercise: A group of mandrills is called a horde. What does horde mean? | A single monkey alone | *A big group | A type of fruit | A kind of grass on the savanna
test: «Rafiki in The Lion King is partly a mandrill.» What does partly mean here? | *In part, but not completely | Completely and fully | Never at all | Only in the dark
test: What do mandrills eat? | *Fruit, seeds and insects | Only grass from the savanna | Fish from the river | Only other monkeys
exam: Which is the largest monkey in the world? | *Mandrill | Spider monkey | Pygmy marmoset | Baboon
